From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] grt: size the maze arrays to the grid
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The maze's distance, parent and region arrays were allocated on a square
of the grid's longer side, and on at least 1000 x 1000 GCells: on a
377 x 542 x 9 grid, d1_3D_, d2_3D_ and path_len_3D_ took 108 MB where
22 MB covers every GCell, and an elongated die paid for the square.
Every access is clamped to the grid and the index arithmetic uses
x_range_ as the row stride, so the arrays are now x_grid_ x y_grid_.

cost_hvh_test_ is indexed along x like cost_hvh_, but was sized by
y_range_, which only held on a square; it is now sized by x_range_.

Carried in bazel-orfs for OpenROAD#12075, not upstreamed; retires with
the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp | 10 +++-------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp b/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp
index 3b9f2e2a8f..27f1625d36 100644
--- a/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp
+++ b/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp
@@ -317,12 +317,8 @@ void FastRouteCore::setGridsAndLayers(int x, int y, int nLayers)
   y_grid_ = y;
   num_layers_ = nLayers;
   layer_directions_.resize(num_layers_);
-  if (std::max(x_grid_, y_grid_) >= 1000) {
-    x_range_ = std::max(x_grid_, y_grid_);
-  } else {
-    x_range_ = 1000;
-  }
-  y_range_ = x_range_;
+  x_range_ = x_grid_;
+  y_range_ = y_grid_;
 
   v_capacity_3D_.resize(num_layers_);
   h_capacity_3D_.resize(num_layers_);
@@ -350,7 +346,7 @@ void FastRouteCore::setGridsAndLayers(int x, int y, int nLayers)
   cost_lr_.resize(y_range_);   // Left and right boundary cost
   cost_tb_.resize(x_range_);   // Top and bottom boundary cost
 
-  cost_hvh_test_.resize(y_range_);  // Vertical first Z
+  cost_hvh_test_.resize(x_range_);  // Horizontal first Z
   cost_v_test_.resize(x_range_);    // Vertical segment cost
   cost_tb_test_.resize(x_range_);   // Top and bottom boundary cost
 
